[gd_scene format=3]

; Dedicated fixture for the runtime NODE-LIFECYCLE integration probe — runtime_node_add
; and runtime_node_remove, ranked #1 on handoff 151 §2's list of runtime tools with no
; live coverage (~44 lines of GDScript, the densest error paths left in the plane).
;
; DELIBERATELY SCRIPTLESS, and that is the design rather than an omission.
;
; Every other probe fixture in this directory carries a script whose _ready() builds the
; state its lane needs. This lane's subject IS the shape of the tree, so anything that
; mutated the tree on boot would be competing with the tool under test: after a failure
; you could not tell whether a node is present because node_add put it there or because
; the fixture did. With no script, EVERY node that appears under this root during the run
; was put there by runtime_node_add, and every one that disappears was taken by
; runtime_node_remove. The probe's pristine-restore check at the end is only meaningful
; because of that.
;
; The two nodes exist for these reasons and no others:
;
;   NodeProbe  Node2D  -> the scene ROOT, which is the subject of _node_remove's
;                         `cannot_remove_root` guard. The probe attacks it by both spellings
;                         that _resolve maps onto the root ("." and "") and then proves it
;                         SURVIVED — a guard that refused and freed anyway would pass a
;                         reply-only check.
;   Host       Node2D  -> a PRE-EXISTING NON-ROOT parent. Adding under it exercises
;                         _resolve + _path_of on a nested parent, which adding under the
;                         root cannot: a _path_of that returned get_path() instead of the
;                         scene-relative path is invisible at the root and wrong here.
;                         Its child_count is also the pristine anchor — 0 at boot, and 0
;                         again when the probe is done.
;
; The PackedScene the `scene:` branch instantiates is a SEPARATE file,
; res://tests/node_payload.tscn — see its header for why it could not be one of these.
;
; Driven headless by the runtime-plane CI job (:9086); see
; host/test-integration/node-lifecycle.integration.mjs.

[node name="NodeProbe" type="Node2D"]

[node name="Host" type="Node2D" parent="."]
